:''This article is about the Worker Cat. For the Cat Unit, go to [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)]]. For the Battle Item, go to [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]].''
[[File:Worker cat.png|thumb|220x220px]]
'''Worker Cat''' is a support cat that creates cash, needed to produce all Cats in the game. At the beginning of each [[Battle]], the Worker Cat starts at Level 1 unless using a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] or certain [[Cat Combo]]s. Worker Cat can be leveled up while in battle, which increases the amount of money that can be held. Leveling Up Worker Cat in battle requires more cash with every level, up to a maximum of Level 8. The formula is: (Level 1 worker cat cost * Current upgrade level = cost to upgrade). Upgrading Worker Cat Rate increases the amount of money you make in a second while making upgrades more expensive. Upgrading Worker Cat Wallet increases the amount of money that can be stored. Certain Treasures can also boost Worker Cat's cash generation speed or maximum money stored.

At level 1, it produces about 170¢ per second, and each level increases speed by about 5% of the previous level.

==Worker Cat Efficiency (upgrade)==
:''Not to be confused with the [[Energy Drink]], a Treasure that boosts Worker Cat's efficiency without a downside.''
The Worker Cat Efficiency is an upgrade that boosts how much money the Worker Cat makes in a second. It also has a downside, in that it increases how much it costs to upgrade the Worker Cat in battle. Unlike the Energy Drink, each time you upgrade the Efficiency with XP, the cost to upgrade Worker Cat in battle by each level increases by 20 cash per upgrade.

==Worker Cat Wallet (upgrade)==
:''Not to be confused with the [[Giant Safe]], a Treasure that boost Worker Cat's wallet.''
Worker Cat's Wallet increases with every upgrade, meaning more maximum cash. It is essential to upgrade Cat Wallet in order to produce more expensive units, like Uber Rares or Super Rares.

